{"code_citation":"O.C.G.A. § 44-3-220","title":"Definitions — Georgia Property Owners' Association Act","category":"amendments","body":"As used in this article, the term 'property owners' association' means a corporation formed for the purpose of exercising the powers of a property owners' association as set forth in this article. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text from law.justia.com/codes/georgia/title-44/chapter-3/article-6/ before production use.","source_url":"https://law.justia.com/codes/georgia/title-44/chapter-3/article-6/","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"O.C.G.A. § 44-3-225","title":"Liens for assessments; foreclosure","category":"foreclosure","body":"Assessments levied by the property owners' association are a continuing lien on each lot. The lien attaches when the assessment becomes due. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use. The lien may be foreclosed in like manner as a mortgage on real estate; the association is entitled to costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","source_url":"https://law.justia.com/codes/georgia/title-44/chapter-3/article-6/","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"O.C.G.A. § 44-3-232","title":"Meetings of association; notice","category":"meetings","body":"The property owners' association shall hold an annual meeting of the members at the time specified in the bylaws. Notice of all meetings, regular or special, shall be given to each lot owner in the manner prescribed in the bylaws, not less than 21 days nor more than 30 days in advance of the meeting. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://law.justia.com/codes/georgia/title-44/chapter-3/article-6/","effective_date":null}
{"code_citation":"O.C.G.A. § 44-3-235","title":"Books and records; right of inspection","category":"records","body":"The property owners' association shall keep books and records of the receipts and expenditures of the association. The books and records shall be available for inspection by any lot owner during reasonable business hours. SAMPLE EXCERPT — replace with full statutory text before production use.","source_url":"https://law.justia.com/codes/georgia/title-44/chapter-3/article-6/","effective_date":null}
